        -:  434:    /**
        -:  435:     * Set the reference designators in the list that have not been annotated.
        -:  436:     *
        -:  437:     * If a the sheet number is 2 and \a aSheetIntervalId is 100, then the first reference
        -:  438:     * designator would be 201 and the last reference designator would be 299 when no overlap
        -:  439:     * occurs with sheet number 3.  If there are 150 items in sheet number 2, then items are
        -:  440:     * referenced U201 to U351, and items in sheet 3 start from U352
        -:  441:     *
        -:  442:     * @param aUseSheetNum Set to true to start annotation for each sheet at the sheet number
        -:  443:     *                     times \a aSheetIntervalId.  Otherwise annotate incrementally.
        -:  444:     * @param aSheetIntervalId The per sheet reference designator multiplier.
        -:  445:     * @param aStartNumber The number to start with if NOT numbering based on sheet number.
        -:  446:     * @param aLockedUnitMap A SCH_MULTI_UNIT_REFERENCE_MAP of reference designator wxStrings
        -:  447:     *      to SCH_REFERENCE_LISTs. May be an empty map. If not empty, any multi-unit parts
        -:  448:     *      found in this map will be annotated as a group rather than individually.
        -:  449:     * @param aAdditionalRefs Additional references to use for checking that there a reference
        -:  450:     *      designator doesn't already exist. The caller must ensure that none of the references
        -:  451:     *      in aAdditionalRefs exist in this list.
        -:  452:     * @param aStartAtCurrent Use m_numRef for each reference as the start number (overrides
        -:  453:            aStartNumber)
